<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Oduduwa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Oduduwa is the legendary progenitor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yoruba">Yoruba peoples</a> and the founding ruler of Ile-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ife">Ife</a> in Yoruba tradition. Many Yoruba dynasties trace their descent from him. According to oral tradition, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oyo-empire">Oyo Empire</a> was founded by his youngest son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oranmiyan">Oranmiyan</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/oduduwa.jpg" alt="Oduduwa" width="315" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tunde Akangbe · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Oduduwa_02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
